# QMS Validation Protocol Generator

Generate EU GMP Annex 15 compliant validation protocols (IQ/OQ/PQ).

## Activation
- User requests: "validation protocol", "IQ", "OQ", "PQ", "qualification", "process validation"

---

<qms-validation-protocol>

## Instructions

You are generating EU GMP Annex 15 compliant validation/qualification protocols for cannabis pharmaceutical operations.

### PROTOCOL TYPES

| Type | Full Name | Purpose | When |
|------|-----------|---------|------|
| DQ | Design Qualification | Verify design meets requirements | Before purchase |
| IQ | Installation Qualification | Verify correct installation | After installation |
| OQ | Operational Qualification | Verify operation within limits | After IQ |
| PQ | Performance Qualification | Verify consistent performance | After OQ |
| PV | Process Validation | Verify process produces quality product | Before routine production |
| CV | Cleaning Validation | Verify cleaning removes residues | Before use |

### EU GMP ANNEX 15 REQUIREMENTS

- <cite source="ANNEX15-3.2">Written protocols specifying how qualification will be conducted</cite>
- <cite source="ANNEX15-3.3">Protocols should include acceptance criteria</cite>
- <cite source="ANNEX15-3.4">Qualification documents may be combined where appropriate</cite>
- <cite source="ANNEX15-5.1">Critical process parameters (CPPs) should be identified</cite>

### PROTOCOL STRUCTURE

#### 1. Cover Page
```markdown
# {Type} Protocol: {Equipment/Process Name}

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Protocol Number | {VAL-XXX-001} |
| Equipment/Process | {name} |
| Equipment ID | {asset number} |
| Location | {room/area} |
| Manufacturer | {manufacturer} |
| Model/Serial | {model} / {serial} |
| Protocol Version | 1.0 |
| Effective Date | {date} |

## Approval Signatures

| Role | Name | Signature | Date |
|------|------|-----------|------|
| Author | __________ | __________ | _____ |
| Reviewer (Engineering) | __________ | __________ | _____ |
| Reviewer (QA) | __________ | __________ | _____ |
| Approver (QA Manager) | __________ | __________ | _____ |
```

#### 2. Purpose and Scope
```markdown
## 1. Purpose

This protocol establishes the procedure for {IQ/OQ/PQ} of the {equipment name} to demonstrate that it is properly {installed/operates/performs} according to specifications and is suitable for its intended use in cannabis pharmaceutical manufacturing.

## 2. Scope

This protocol applies to:
- Equipment: {name and ID}
- Location: {room}
- Processes: {associated processes}

Out of scope:
- {items not covered}
```

#### 3. References
```markdown
## 3. References

| Document | Title |
|----------|-------|
| EU GMP Annex 15 | Qualification and Validation |
| SOP-VAL-001 | Validation Master Plan |
| SOP-EQP-XXX | Equipment Operation SOP |
| URS-XXX | User Requirements Specification |
| Vendor Manual | {manufacturer documentation} |
```

#### 4. Responsibilities
```markdown
## 4. Responsibilities

| Role | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| Validation Lead | Execute protocol, document results |
| Engineering | Technical support, equipment access |
| QA | Review/approve protocol and report |
| Production | Witness testing, provide input |
```

#### 5. Prerequisites (IQ/OQ/PQ specific)
```markdown
## 5. Prerequisites

### For IQ:
- [ ] Purchase order received
- [ ] Site preparation complete
- [ ] Utilities available (power, water, compressed air)
- [ ] Vendor documentation received

### For OQ:
- [ ] IQ approved
- [ ] Calibrated instruments available
- [ ] Operating SOP draft available
- [ ] Training completed

### For PQ:
- [ ] OQ approved
- [ ] Production materials available
- [ ] Trained operators available
- [ ] Sampling plan approved
```

#### 6. Test Sections

##### IQ Tests
```markdown
## 6. Installation Qualification Tests

### 6.1 Documentation Verification
| Test ID | Item | Expected | Actual | Pass/Fail |
|---------|------|----------|--------|-----------|
| IQ-001 | Purchase Order | On file | ☐ Verified | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-002 | Vendor Manual | Received | ☐ Verified | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-003 | Certificates (CE, calibration) | Received | ☐ Verified | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-004 | Spare Parts List | On file | ☐ Verified | ☐ P ☐ F |

### 6.2 Physical Verification
| Test ID | Item | Specification | Actual | Pass/Fail |
|---------|------|---------------|--------|-----------|
| IQ-005 | Equipment ID tag | {ID} installed | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-006 | Location | Room {XXX} | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-007 | Model number | {model} | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-008 | Serial number | {serial} | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F |

### 6.3 Utility Verification
| Test ID | Utility | Requirement | Actual | Pass/Fail |
|---------|---------|-------------|--------|-----------|
| IQ-009 | Electrical | {voltage} | _____ V | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-010 | Compressed Air | {pressure} | _____ bar | ☐ P ☐ F |
| IQ-011 | Water | Purified Water | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F |
```

##### OQ Tests
